### Audio for d2s (Exynos 9825): plain ALSA, NOT module-droid-card.
###
### droid.pa includes this file in place of its own
###     load-module module-droid-card rate=48000
### line, so whatever is loaded here is what provides the primary sink.
###
###
### WHY module-droid-card IS NOT USED
###
### It cannot work on this device, and no argument to it would have helped.
### The only real audio HAL is /vendor/lib/hw/audio.primary.exynos9825.so and
### it is 32-bit ONLY. So is /vendor/bin/hw/android.hardware.audio@2.0-service,
### which is why Samsung never built a 64-bit one. /vendor/lib64/hw/ contains
### only the AOSP stub (audio.primary.default.so, "Default audio HW HAL",
### 15 KB, links no implementation) and a 15 KB Samsung shim
### (audio.sec_primary.default.so) that itself needs the missing 32-bit
### implementation.
###
### Sailfish's PulseAudio is 64-bit and a 64-bit process cannot dlopen a
### 32-bit library. module-droid-card therefore reached nothing but the stub,
### which accepts streams, reports success and discards the audio - PulseAudio
### looked perfectly healthy, routed correctly, applied volume, and the device
### was silent. That also explains the EINVAL that went unexplained for a long
### time: the Samsung shim loads the primary HAL, gets the stub, logs
### "The audio hal does not support to samsung audio hal" and returns -EINVAL.
###
###
### WHY hw:0,1 AND NOT hw:0,0
###
### RDMA0 (hw:0,0) is the obvious choice and it is broken. The Calliope DSP
### accepts the whole sequence - opens the channel, allocates the entity
### buffer, takes the hw_params and the start trigger, logs no error - and then
### never sends PCM_PLTDAI_POINTER back. abox_rdma_pointer() only advances when
### that message arrives, so hw_ptr sits at 0 while appl_ptr climbs and ALSA
### eventually fails the write with EIO. Not a format problem: every channel
### and width combination behaves identically, and mmap access hangs instead of
### erroring.
###
### RDMA1 and several others are fine. Scanning every playback device, only
### RDMA0 and RDMA4 fail. On RDMA1 the pointer advances normally and the
### cs35l41 amps report real cone excursion (0.3899) and voice-coil heating,
### i.e. the speakers physically move. ABOX SPUS OUT1 is already routed to
### SIFS0 by the initial mixer block, so RDMA1 reaches the speaker amps by the
### same path RDMA0 would have.
###
###
### The sink MUST be called sink.primary-out. Sailfish's routing tables
### (/etc/pulse/x-maemo-route.table, xpolicy.conf) and module-policy-enforcement
### address the primary output by that name; renaming it leaves every stream
### routed at a sink that no longer exists.
###
### tsched=0 because the ABOX DMA reports position by DSP message rather than
### by a free-running hardware counter, which is not a good fit for PulseAudio's
### timer-based scheduling. Explicit fragments keep the period at 4096 frames.
###
### Routing comes from droid-alsa-mixer.service, which applies Samsung's own
### media-dual-speaker path. Without it this sink opens cleanly and is still
### silent, because nothing has connected SIFS0 to the amps.
###
###
### WHY THE droid.output.* PROPERTIES
###
### The name alone is not enough. module-policy-enforcement resolves devices
### by sink PROPERTY, not by name - /etc/pulse/xpolicy.conf defines the
### loudspeaker as
###     [device]
###     type = ihf
###     sink = $output_media_latency@equals:$output_equals
### i.e. "the sink whose droid.output.media_latency is true". module-droid-card
### sets those properties; module-alsa-sink sets none (only device.api=alsa),
### so the ihf device matched no sink and every group that follows the route
### (player, game, ...) was parked on the fallback sink.null. Observed on
### device: ringtones and system sounds still played, media did not, and PA
### logged
###     force stream 'player'/... to sink 'sink.null'
### with every later route update reporting "identical, no need to move
### streams". Declaring the properties makes the ihf rule resolve to this sink.
load-module module-alsa-sink device=hw:0,1 sink_name=sink.primary-out rate=48000 channels=2 format=s16le tsched=0 fragments=4 fragment_size=4096 sink_properties="droid.output.primary=true droid.output.media_latency=true droid.output.low_latency=true"

### MICROPHONE
###
### hw:0,13 is ABOX WDMA1, fed from the codec's UAIF0 by the controls in
### /usr/share/droid-audio/mixer-mic-main.tsv (applied at boot by
### droid-alsa-mixer.service). Without that routing this source opens and
### records silence.
###
### droid.input.builtin=true for the same reason the sink carries droid.output.*:
### xpolicy.conf picks the built-in microphone as
###     source = $input_builtin@equals:$input_equals
### i.e. "the source whose droid.input.builtin is true". Without it recording
### streams (Recorder, camera video) are routed to source.null and capture
### nothing.
load-module module-alsa-source device=hw:0,13 source_name=source.primary rate=48000 channels=2 format=s16le tsched=0 fragments=4 fragment_size=4096 source_properties="droid.input.builtin=true"
